1
00:00:04,651 --> 00:00:06,570
THE FOLLOWING CONTENT CONTAINS DEPICTIONS
OF CHILD MALTREATMENT.

2
00:00:06,653 --> 00:00:07,654
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

3
00:00:08,614 --> 00:00:10,073
-[Aunt A] Heeju!
-[Sunok] Heeju!

4
00:00:10,157 --> 00:00:13,535
-[Mija] Heeju!
-[Aunt B] Heeju, where are you?

5
00:00:13,618 --> 00:00:16,371
-[Aunt B] Heeju!
-[Aunt A] Heeju! Heeju!

6
00:00:17,039 --> 00:00:19,374
[Aunt A] Sunok, Sunok! Heeju!

7
00:00:19,458 --> 00:00:22,461
[all speaking at once]

8
00:00:24,171 --> 00:00:26,590
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

9
00:00:26,673 --> 00:00:28,091
[women gasping]

10
00:00:28,175 --> 00:00:29,968
How do we get down there?

11
00:00:30,052 --> 00:00:31,303
[all gasping]

12
00:00:31,386 --> 00:00:33,430
-[Mija] Heeju, it's me, Auntie Mija.
-I swear she's nothing but trouble.

13
00:00:33,513 --> 00:00:34,556
[Mija] Right here!

14
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,807
[Aunt B] Are you okay?

15
00:00:35,891 --> 00:00:38,268
-[Mija] How can we get her out of there?
-[Aunt B] What do we do?

16
00:00:38,352 --> 00:00:40,312
[Sunok] You've got no idea how dangerous
this place is.

17
00:00:40,395 --> 00:00:42,856
Fine then, go on.
Get back in there.

18
00:00:42,939 --> 00:00:44,650
[Heeju] This woman is my mother.

19
00:00:45,734 --> 00:00:47,861
"Nothing but bad luck."

20
00:00:48,904 --> 00:00:51,239
That's what my mom always called me.

21
00:00:52,491 --> 00:00:55,327
I thought my mom's misfortune
was because of me.

22
00:00:56,411 --> 00:00:58,372
And so I always felt guilty.

23
00:00:59,456 --> 00:01:02,167
At the time,
I didn't understand what that meant.

24
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:05,754
[9-Year-Old Heeju and Sunok crying]

25
00:01:05,837 --> 00:01:08,757
[indistinct chatter]

26
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:11,843
[♪ melancholy music]

27
00:01:23,438 --> 00:01:25,774
[Heeju] Spellbound by
the dazzling lights...

28
00:01:26,608 --> 00:01:29,319
...people streamed endlessly
toward Gold Land.

29
00:01:29,403 --> 00:01:32,656
[slot machines chiming and clicking]

30
00:01:32,739 --> 00:01:35,701
They say not everything that glitters
is gold.

31
00:01:35,784 --> 00:01:39,579
In the end,
it was nothing more than a gilded grave.

32
00:01:49,214 --> 00:01:52,801
Maybe my mother was dazzled
by those lights, too,

33
00:01:52,884 --> 00:01:55,512
wagering everything she had.

34
00:01:55,595 --> 00:01:57,222
[Croupier] Player, banker.

35
00:01:57,305 --> 00:01:58,974
[Heeju] Hoping for
a single stroke of luck.

36
00:02:01,268 --> 00:02:05,564
Unfortunately, luck is never fair, is it?

37
00:02:06,648 --> 00:02:08,108
[Croupier] Final bets.

38
00:02:11,445 --> 00:02:12,946
-Ah.
-[Croupier] Out.

39
00:02:13,029 --> 00:02:14,406
-[Sunok grunts]
-[Croupier] You fold?

40
00:02:14,489 --> 00:02:16,700
-House wins.
-[Sunok] I can't believe this.

41
00:02:16,783 --> 00:02:20,120
-[man groans]
-[Sunok exhales sharply]

42
00:02:20,203 --> 00:02:23,206
[bus engine rumbling]

43
00:02:23,290 --> 00:02:28,462
13, JEONGSAN BUS TERMINAL
SEOKWOL-DONG

44
00:02:29,504 --> 00:02:32,466
[brakes hissing]

45
00:02:37,012 --> 00:02:39,473
[door closes]

46
00:02:40,390 --> 00:02:42,017
Did you eat yet?

47
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:43,101
Ramyeon.

48
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:51,943
[bag rustling]

49
00:02:54,196 --> 00:02:55,822
[food crunching]

50
00:02:58,074 --> 00:02:59,618
I wanna go to school, Mom.

51
00:03:00,619 --> 00:03:04,623
Da In gets to go to school
and she's a year younger than me.

52
00:03:07,209 --> 00:03:08,460
You can go next year.

53
00:03:10,670 --> 00:03:11,713
Not here, though.

54
00:03:13,006 --> 00:03:14,925
You can go in Seoul.

55
00:03:15,008 --> 00:03:16,468
Really?

56
00:03:17,969 --> 00:03:20,388
Yes. Really.

57
00:03:21,848 --> 00:03:23,016
[exhales]

58
00:03:23,099 --> 00:03:25,268
I just can't live in
this place any longer.
STYLE
::cue()

59
00:03:27,354 --> 00:03:28,563
We'll go to Seoul.

60
00:03:32,192 --> 00:03:33,944
[crunching]

61
00:03:34,027 --> 00:03:36,780
[Heeju] As always, it was just a lie.

62
00:03:38,490 --> 00:03:42,160
But even if it was a lie,
I wanted to believe it.

63
00:03:42,244 --> 00:03:45,038
THE CITY OF DREAMS AND HOPE
WELCOME TO GOLD LAND

64
00:03:45,121 --> 00:03:48,667
HIGH-VALUE LOANS, HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP
LENDING, PURCHASING

65
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:54,965
GOLD, SILVER, JEWELRY, WATCHES
TOP PRICES PAID FOR GOLD

66
00:03:55,048 --> 00:03:58,134
-[Cheoljung] Come here.
-[Heeju] Instead of leaving like she said,

67
00:03:58,218 --> 00:04:00,679
my mother got married
to the pawnshop owner.

68
00:04:00,762 --> 00:04:04,724
On the condition
that he paid off her debt.

69
00:04:04,808 --> 00:04:09,771
Both me and my mother
were like collateral at his shop.

70
00:04:10,689 --> 00:04:14,359
[clock loudly echoing]
[Sunok] I said cut it out.

71
00:04:14,442 --> 00:04:16,903
[Man on Street] Slow down.
Be careful, kids.

72
00:04:16,987 --> 00:04:19,990
[children laughing and shouting]

73
00:04:24,786 --> 00:04:29,791
[Heeju] A heart with no destination
to go always lets the feet know first.

74
00:04:31,835 --> 00:04:33,753
For many years I was stuck,

75
00:04:33,837 --> 00:04:36,840
walking down a road I never wanted
to return to.

76
00:04:37,966 --> 00:04:42,304
I prayed every day that my destination
would be somewhere else.

77
00:04:43,889 --> 00:04:48,059
In reality, the dream
that felt so far away

78
00:04:48,143 --> 00:04:51,187
only grew closer and more familiar.

79
00:04:52,022 --> 00:04:56,318
[Male Singer] ♪ All the things
I thought I could be ♪

80
00:04:57,527 --> 00:04:59,779
♪ Wild and free ♪

81
00:05:01,990 --> 00:05:06,453
♪ Leave it all behind ♪

82
00:05:06,536 --> 00:05:10,749
♪ As you fall in line ♪

83
00:05:10,832 --> 00:05:15,003
♪ I'm not expecting any laughter ♪

84
00:05:15,086 --> 00:05:16,880
♪ There's nothing left ♪

85
00:05:16,963 --> 00:05:22,969
♪ Just the pieces of everything
we could have been before ♪

86
00:05:23,053 --> 00:05:26,765
♪ Evermore ♪

87
00:05:27,599 --> 00:05:33,104
♪ I don't feel it like I used to ♪

88
00:05:33,188 --> 00:05:35,732
♪ Anymore ♪

89
00:05:39,110 --> 00:05:43,448
[Heeju] My mother was like a plant
that could no longer bloom,

90
00:05:43,531 --> 00:05:44,866
slowly withering away.

91
00:05:46,618 --> 00:05:48,662
The thought that I could end up
like her...

92
00:05:50,372 --> 00:05:51,539
...It terrified me.

93
00:05:52,916 --> 00:05:56,086
[Male Singer] ♪ Still calling through
the night ♪

94
00:05:57,504 --> 00:06:01,216
♪ I leave behind all of the seasons... ♪

95
00:06:01,299 --> 00:06:04,886
[Heeju] At Haengbok Pawnshop,
there is no happiness.

96
00:06:06,554 --> 00:06:10,100
Only someone's collateral,
held like hostages.

97
00:06:10,183 --> 00:06:11,977
[distant jet engine roaring]

98
00:06:12,060 --> 00:06:14,354
[Heeju] If only I could
fly somewhere else.

99
00:06:15,271 --> 00:06:16,523
How nice would it be?

100
00:06:17,232 --> 00:06:18,441
Anywhere.

101
00:06:18,525 --> 00:06:20,235
Anywhere but here.

102
00:06:22,028 --> 00:06:24,322
[Male Singer] ♪ On your own ♪

103
00:06:25,824 --> 00:06:27,117
[Heeju] Sometimes in the evenings,

104
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:29,744
the pawnshop became
a gambling den.

105
00:06:29,828 --> 00:06:32,831
[indistinct chatter]

106
00:06:38,628 --> 00:06:41,423
Soju there, cigarettes here.
We have to sell it all.

107
00:06:41,506 --> 00:06:43,174
[Man in Pawnshop A] Bring it here!

108
00:06:49,639 --> 00:06:50,640
[exhales sharply]
STYLE
::cue()

109
00:06:59,315 --> 00:07:00,942
[exhales]

110
00:07:29,137 --> 00:07:30,680
[locker and chains rattle]

111
00:07:35,769 --> 00:07:36,895
[exhales]

112
00:07:39,689 --> 00:07:41,524
[chains rattling]

113
00:07:43,193 --> 00:07:44,277
[lock clicks]

114
00:07:46,070 --> 00:07:47,447
[lock clicking]

115
00:07:49,532 --> 00:07:50,950
[gasps]

116
00:07:58,249 --> 00:08:01,586
[chains clinking]

117
00:08:01,669 --> 00:08:04,297
[lock squeaking]

118
00:08:13,306 --> 00:08:15,141
[door opens]

119
00:08:15,225 --> 00:08:16,559
[locker creaks]

120
00:08:17,811 --> 00:08:18,978
[Man in Pawnshop B] Mr. Han.

121
00:08:19,062 --> 00:08:20,897
I said I'd give it to you by next week!

122
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:22,190
[Cheoljung] So you keep saying.

123
00:08:23,191 --> 00:08:25,693
[Cheoljung] I trust money, not words.

124
00:08:26,444 --> 00:08:29,697
[Cheoljung] People say they'll
pay back billions, even trillions.

125
00:08:29,781 --> 00:08:31,866
[whimpering]

126
00:08:33,493 --> 00:08:35,870
[crying]

127
00:08:35,954 --> 00:08:37,705
What's wrong?

128
00:08:38,373 --> 00:08:40,375
Is your little heart pounding?

129
00:08:40,458 --> 00:08:43,586
I could cut you open
for screwing me out of my money.

130
00:08:43,670 --> 00:08:45,338
[Cheoljung] Is that what
you're worried about?

131
00:08:54,264 --> 00:08:55,765
[whimpers]

132
00:08:57,809 --> 00:09:00,687
[Cheoljung] Look here.
You see that?

133
00:09:00,770 --> 00:09:03,815
It's easy to control
it when it's my own flesh.

134
00:09:03,898 --> 00:09:07,360
[Cheoljung] But on someone else's,
not so much.

135
00:09:07,443 --> 00:09:12,031
That's why I always cut myself first
to show you.

136
00:09:12,115 --> 00:09:14,993
[muffled wailing]

137
00:09:16,452 --> 00:09:17,495
[gasps]

138
00:09:18,746 --> 00:09:20,415
[panicked breathing]

139
00:09:20,999 --> 00:09:22,250
[lock clicks]

140
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:23,877
[gasps]

141
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:26,713
[door lock beeping]

142
00:09:26,796 --> 00:09:28,089
[door creaks open]

143
00:10:01,915 --> 00:10:03,291
What are you doing here?

144
00:10:06,252 --> 00:10:08,046
Just my homework.

145
00:10:08,129 --> 00:10:09,214
[Heeju] I guess I fell asleep.

146
00:10:10,131 --> 00:10:12,175
Oh, really?

147
00:10:13,134 --> 00:10:14,344
[Heeju gasps]

148
00:10:15,678 --> 00:10:17,513
[panicked breathing]

149
00:10:19,807 --> 00:10:22,352
[whimpering]
STYLE
::cue()

150
00:10:22,435 --> 00:10:24,187
-[Heeju screams]
-[Cheoljung grunts]

151
00:10:26,189 --> 00:10:27,315
[gasps]

152
00:10:29,275 --> 00:10:31,110
-[Heeju screams]
-[wailing]

153
00:10:31,194 --> 00:10:34,030
-[Cheoljung groaning]
-[panicked breathing]

154
00:10:35,949 --> 00:10:37,992
[Cheoljung] Heeju!

155
00:10:38,076 --> 00:10:40,536
[pained groaning]

156
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:44,374
[breathing heavily]

157
00:11:02,350 --> 00:11:04,644
-[Sunok] Where are you?
-[Heeju] I'm leaving this place.

158
00:11:04,727 --> 00:11:08,398
I won't go back. That man is crazy.
He's not even human. I'm too scared to.

159
00:11:08,481 --> 00:11:09,732
[Sunok] Where else would you go?

160
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:12,610
Anywhere. I don't know.

161
00:11:13,486 --> 00:11:15,321
[Sunok] You got any money?

162
00:11:15,405 --> 00:11:17,031
How are you gonna survive on your own?

163
00:11:17,907 --> 00:11:20,576
I don't know.
I'll figure it out.

164
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:23,079
And you?
You're okay living like this?

165
00:11:23,162 --> 00:11:25,373
You actually think he sees me
as his niece?

166
00:11:27,041 --> 00:11:29,002
[Sunok] Go and stay with Mija for a while.

167
00:11:29,794 --> 00:11:32,130
When your uncle cools off,
you can come back.

168
00:11:32,213 --> 00:11:34,257
[groaning]

169
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:37,885
No, Mom, why can't we
just leave this place?

170
00:11:39,887 --> 00:11:40,888
[Sunok] Don't call me Mom.

171
00:11:43,516 --> 00:11:44,851
[phone receiver clicks]

172
00:11:44,934 --> 00:11:46,436
[Heeju] Oh, that's right.

173
00:11:47,687 --> 00:11:48,980
I don't have a mother.

174
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:52,108
I almost forgot.

175
00:11:52,191 --> 00:11:57,238
I'm nothing but an utterly luckless brat.

176
00:12:00,408 --> 00:12:01,868
[phone receiver rattles]

177
00:12:04,704 --> 00:12:07,623
[Heeju crying]

178
00:12:15,548 --> 00:12:18,551
[crying continues]

179
00:12:22,722 --> 00:12:25,725
[♪ sad music]

180
00:12:45,536 --> 00:12:48,539
[♪ music continues]

181
00:13:03,930 --> 00:13:11,270
EPISODE 2
HOMECOMING

182
00:13:18,403 --> 00:13:19,404
[exhales]

183
00:13:39,882 --> 00:13:41,467
[phone trilling]

184
00:13:41,551 --> 00:13:44,303
[exhales sharply]

185
00:13:44,387 --> 00:13:46,139
Uh, hi there.

186
00:13:46,222 --> 00:13:51,227
Last night there was a car accident on
National Route 6 around midnight, I think.

187
00:13:52,145 --> 00:13:54,814
Have there been any reports
of the accident yet?
STYLE
::cue()

188
00:13:58,901 --> 00:14:00,778
[inhales and exhales sharply]

189
00:14:00,862 --> 00:14:02,864
Could you tell me what hospital he's in?

190
00:14:02,947 --> 00:14:05,616
[Female Police Officer] May I have
the name of the person calling?

191
00:14:06,534 --> 00:14:07,535
I...

192
00:14:09,579 --> 00:14:11,122
[shudders]

193
00:14:11,831 --> 00:14:12,915
[phone beeps]

194
00:14:13,958 --> 00:14:14,959
[exhales]

195
00:14:17,628 --> 00:14:18,796
[breathes heavily]

196
00:14:22,884 --> 00:14:24,177
[gasps]

197
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:25,511
[Heeju] There isn't?

198
00:14:26,012 --> 00:14:27,346
Okay, thank you.

199
00:14:27,430 --> 00:14:28,806
[phone beeps]

200
00:14:30,683 --> 00:14:31,809
[phone chimes]

201
00:14:31,893 --> 00:14:33,686
[trilling]

202
00:14:33,769 --> 00:14:35,605
[inhales sharply]
Hello.

203
00:14:35,688 --> 00:14:38,524
I'm calling to check on a patient who
was brought to the ER after

204
00:14:38,608 --> 00:14:41,110
a car accident around midnight last night.
It's a man...

205
00:14:41,194 --> 00:14:43,696
[Female Security Officer] Hey, Heeju!
Heeju!

206
00:14:43,779 --> 00:14:45,156
They want all of us in the office.

207
00:14:45,656 --> 00:14:46,657
Why?

208
00:14:46,741 --> 00:14:48,201
[Female Security Officer] The police
are here now.

209
00:14:48,284 --> 00:14:50,119
They have some questions for all of us.

210
00:14:50,203 --> 00:14:52,330
[Female Security Officer] Ms. Cha, too.
We gotta go.

211
00:14:52,413 --> 00:14:53,414
Sure.

212
00:14:59,045 --> 00:15:00,963
[door opens]
[mouse button clicks]

213
00:15:01,047 --> 00:15:02,381
[Male Detective A] What is that?

214
00:15:03,382 --> 00:15:05,343
That can't be normal, can it?

215
00:15:06,761 --> 00:15:10,139
Yesterday, who was-who was in charge
of the scanner?

216
00:15:10,223 --> 00:15:12,183
Uh, I was.

217
00:15:12,266 --> 00:15:14,352
The warning alarm went off, right?

218
00:15:14,435 --> 00:15:16,687
Aren't you supposed to request
a physical inspection from customs?

219
00:15:16,771 --> 00:15:20,066
Uh, sir, well...

220
00:15:20,149 --> 00:15:21,609
She reported it to me.

221
00:15:21,692 --> 00:15:24,028
As the one in charge, I review
all anomalies and make the final call.

222
00:15:24,111 --> 00:15:27,406
A visual inspection by an expert
is considered the most accurate method.

223
00:15:27,490 --> 00:15:29,367
The alarms are always going off.

224
00:15:29,450 --> 00:15:30,993
And for inbound cargo,

225
00:15:31,077 --> 00:15:33,204
physical inspections
are deemed unnecessary unless

226
00:15:33,287 --> 00:15:34,288
it's an emergency.

227
00:15:34,372 --> 00:15:36,207
This is because it's already been through

228
00:15:36,290 --> 00:15:38,626
a thorough screening
at the outbound checkpoint,

229
00:15:38,709 --> 00:15:40,920
especially when transporting a casket
with a dead body.

230
00:15:41,003 --> 00:15:42,171
[Male Detective A exhales sharply]

231
00:15:42,255 --> 00:15:44,340
[sighs]
So what kind of goods

232
00:15:44,423 --> 00:15:46,342
were they supposedly smuggling?

233
00:15:46,425 --> 00:15:48,636
Ma'am, we never said anything
about smuggling.

234
00:15:48,719 --> 00:15:52,014
The police wouldn't be making such
a fuss if it was for anything else.

235
00:15:53,266 --> 00:15:55,393
[Male Detective B]
Look, you all know this man, right?

236
00:15:55,476 --> 00:15:57,186
San Air first officer Lee Dokyung.

237
00:15:57,270 --> 00:15:59,647
Yeah, I've seen him around a few times.

238
00:15:59,730 --> 00:16:01,148
[Male Detective B] Have you been
in touch recently?

239
00:16:01,232 --> 00:16:02,525
Maybe the last few days?

240
00:16:02,608 --> 00:16:03,776
[Yujin] No.

241
00:16:03,859 --> 00:16:05,111
[Male Detective B]
What about everyone else?

242
00:16:07,905 --> 00:16:11,284
This airport's tiny, so,
weird no one knows him.

243
00:16:11,367 --> 00:16:15,955
Are you asking about the captain because
he's somehow connected to all this?

244
00:16:16,038 --> 00:16:18,291
No, not quite.
It's not like that.

245
00:16:18,374 --> 00:16:19,583
Oh.

246
00:16:21,043 --> 00:16:23,963
Heeju, you were working
at the arrivals terminal.

247
00:16:24,046 --> 00:16:25,339
You must know him.

248
00:16:25,423 --> 00:16:27,300
You would have handled security
for inbound crew.

249
00:16:29,051 --> 00:16:30,052
Yeah.

250
00:16:30,136 --> 00:16:31,470
[cell phone vibrates]
[Male Detective B] I see.

251
00:16:31,554 --> 00:16:32,972
Have you been in contact recently?

252
00:16:33,806 --> 00:16:37,768
Well, it's not like we keep in touch
or anything like that.

253
00:16:37,852 --> 00:16:40,521
We just say hello when
he went through security.

254
00:16:40,604 --> 00:16:41,772
Understood.

255
00:16:41,856 --> 00:16:43,357
-It's Dokyung. They found him.
-Well, where is he?

256
00:16:43,441 --> 00:16:44,984
[Detective Kang]
He's at Yangpo Jeil Hospital.

257
00:16:45,067 --> 00:16:47,153
[Male Detective A] All right,
thanks everyone.

258
00:16:47,236 --> 00:16:48,612
We'll be in touch.

259
00:16:57,580 --> 00:16:58,581
Heeju, wait a minute.

260
00:17:00,583 --> 00:17:02,585
Can I speak with you?

261
00:17:02,668 --> 00:17:05,671
[machines beeping and hissing]

262
00:17:13,554 --> 00:17:14,805
[Male Doctor] Prep the patient
for surgery.

263
00:17:14,889 --> 00:17:15,890
[Nurses] Yes, Doctor.
STYLE
::cue()

264
00:17:20,895 --> 00:17:23,564
[Yujin] So how long have you been close
with Lee Dokyung?

265
00:17:24,732 --> 00:17:25,858
[Heeju] What?

266
00:17:25,941 --> 00:17:27,401
This isn't your first time, is it?

267
00:17:28,527 --> 00:17:30,196
Smuggling goods.

268
00:17:31,113 --> 00:17:33,866
Uh, Ms. Cha, I'm not sure exactly
what you're trying to say.

269
00:17:33,949 --> 00:17:34,992
[Yujin] Fine.

270
00:17:35,076 --> 00:17:36,661
First time or not,

271
00:17:36,744 --> 00:17:38,913
keep your mouth shut
and pretend you don't know anything.

272
00:17:38,996 --> 00:17:42,708
If you're caught by the police,
you understand you and I are both done?

273
00:17:42,792 --> 00:17:43,959
[exhales]

274
00:17:48,631 --> 00:17:50,883
Send me your resignation letter tonight.

275
00:17:50,966 --> 00:17:52,843
And don't come into work tomorrow.

276
00:17:52,927 --> 00:17:55,721
[Yujin] I'll talk to the company
and sort things out.

277
00:17:56,931 --> 00:17:59,850
Once the police wrap up
their investigation,

278
00:17:59,934 --> 00:18:01,185
someone will have to take the fall.

279
00:18:02,019 --> 00:18:04,230
[Yujin] I don't know what's going on
between you two,

280
00:18:04,313 --> 00:18:05,523
but our best hope...

281
00:18:07,608 --> 00:18:10,444
...Is that Lee Dokyung goes and dies.

282
00:18:20,371 --> 00:18:22,790
[inhales and exhales deeply]

283
00:18:23,749 --> 00:18:26,752
[car approaching]

284
00:18:38,681 --> 00:18:40,891
[Female Nurse C] Is Mr. Lee Dokyung's
guardian here?

285
00:18:41,642 --> 00:18:42,685
[Hocheol] Here.

286
00:18:43,185 --> 00:18:44,603
[Female Nurse C] Looks like
the surgery went well.

287
00:18:45,521 --> 00:18:47,523
Mr. Lee is now in recovery.

288
00:18:47,606 --> 00:18:49,692
He's in room 3103.

289
00:18:50,985 --> 00:18:52,611
Is he awake yet?

290
00:18:52,695 --> 00:18:54,071
[Female Nurse C] Uh...

291
00:18:55,865 --> 00:18:59,076
[screaming]

292
00:19:00,286 --> 00:19:01,996
[Female Nurse C]
It usually takes about an hour

293
00:19:02,079 --> 00:19:05,791
or two for the anesthesia to wear off,
so he's still asleep.

294
00:19:05,875 --> 00:19:07,710
You can't see him yet.

295
00:19:07,793 --> 00:19:09,670
Sir, he still needs to rest!

296
00:19:10,755 --> 00:19:14,550
[clock ticking rapidly]

297
00:19:15,551 --> 00:19:18,554
[distant keyboard clacking]

298
00:19:18,637 --> 00:19:21,640
[door creaking]

299
00:19:39,033 --> 00:19:40,451
[gasps]

300
00:19:41,827 --> 00:19:44,163
[panicked breathing]

301
00:19:44,246 --> 00:19:47,249
[cell phone vibrates]

302
00:19:51,837 --> 00:19:52,963
[Detective Kang] Yeah.

303
00:19:53,047 --> 00:19:55,007
[Detective Kang] Yeah, I'll head down
to the first floor.

304
00:19:55,090 --> 00:19:56,133
Okay.

305
00:20:04,016 --> 00:20:05,184
[exhales]

306
00:20:09,313 --> 00:20:12,566
[gasping]

307
00:20:13,234 --> 00:20:14,485
Dokyung.

308
00:20:16,695 --> 00:20:18,447
Wake up.
It's me, Heeju.

309
00:20:19,114 --> 00:20:20,366
Dokyung, can you hear me?

310
00:20:21,534 --> 00:20:23,536
[Heeju breathing erratically]

311
00:20:23,619 --> 00:20:24,662
[Heeju] Dokyung.

312
00:20:27,832 --> 00:20:29,542
[groans]

313
00:20:29,625 --> 00:20:31,335
[Heeju] Dokyung, can you hear me?

314
00:20:32,169 --> 00:20:35,673
[labored breathing]

315
00:20:38,342 --> 00:20:40,261
-[Dokyung] Heeju.
-[exhales sharply]

316
00:20:40,344 --> 00:20:42,805
[Dokyung] I told you not to come here,
didn't I?

317
00:20:43,347 --> 00:20:45,307
I said I'd contact you.

318
00:20:45,391 --> 00:20:47,309
It's okay.
I managed to sneak in.

319
00:20:48,435 --> 00:20:49,687
[exhales]

320
00:20:50,771 --> 00:20:52,022
And the van?

321
00:20:53,357 --> 00:20:54,984
Don't worry. I hid it.

322
00:20:55,067 --> 00:20:56,986
Somewhere no one will know.

323
00:20:57,611 --> 00:20:59,071
-Where's that?
-[Heeju] In Jeongsan,

324
00:20:59,154 --> 00:21:00,865
in the abandoned mines.
STYLE
::cue()

325
00:21:00,948 --> 00:21:03,951
I left it deep in the tunnels
where no one goes anymore.

326
00:21:05,870 --> 00:21:07,872
-[groans]
-[exhales]

327
00:21:07,955 --> 00:21:10,708
[pained groaning]

328
00:21:10,791 --> 00:21:11,792
You did it.

329
00:21:12,877 --> 00:21:14,086
You did it, Heeju.

330
00:21:16,463 --> 00:21:18,465
I'll take care of everything from here.

331
00:21:19,216 --> 00:21:20,384
You should go now.

332
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:22,720
I'm okay. You can go.

333
00:21:25,347 --> 00:21:27,808
The police came to the airport today.

334
00:21:28,934 --> 00:21:30,185
The police? Why?

335
00:21:31,937 --> 00:21:36,066
Well, it looks like they think you were
involved in smuggling in that casket,

336
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:39,194
and they also know you're in the hospital
because of a car accident. Also...

337
00:21:40,738 --> 00:21:43,741
...those men who hit you with the car,

338
00:21:43,824 --> 00:21:44,950
they're here waiting for you.
I saw them.

339
00:21:46,368 --> 00:21:47,870
[exhales sharply]

340
00:21:47,953 --> 00:21:48,954
[Heeju] Let's turn ourselves in.

341
00:21:49,038 --> 00:21:51,248
If we confess to the police now,

342
00:21:51,332 --> 00:21:52,833
the charges might not be that bad.

343
00:21:52,917 --> 00:21:54,460
The police aren't the problem, Heeju.

344
00:21:56,837 --> 00:21:58,839
It's the men you saw outside.

345
00:22:00,132 --> 00:22:02,384
If I were to tell the police
where their drugs are located...

346
00:22:03,302 --> 00:22:05,512
-...Those guys would...
-But it's not drugs.

347
00:22:05,596 --> 00:22:07,181
What?

348
00:22:07,264 --> 00:22:09,308
That's not what's in the casket.

349
00:22:09,391 --> 00:22:11,185
It's not drugs at all.

350
00:22:11,268 --> 00:22:13,938
[gasps]
Then what is it?

351
00:22:15,356 --> 00:22:16,607
Gold bars.

352
00:22:18,776 --> 00:22:22,321
There are a whole bunch of gold bars
that say 10 kilograms on them.

353
00:22:22,404 --> 00:22:24,573
[Heeju] I didn't count,
but there has to be 100.

354
00:22:27,034 --> 00:22:30,788
100 ten-kilogram gold bars?

355
00:22:31,664 --> 00:22:32,831
You're positive?

356
00:22:34,083 --> 00:22:36,794
-[Dokyung] Did you see them yourself?
-Yeah.

357
00:22:36,877 --> 00:22:38,253
Wait a minute.

358
00:22:41,298 --> 00:22:45,052
You mean-you mean there's a ton of gold?

359
00:22:47,262 --> 00:22:49,765
But we should just return it.

360
00:22:49,848 --> 00:22:51,308
If they'll go this far to get it,

361
00:22:51,392 --> 00:22:53,435
then you should just give
it back to them, right?

362
00:22:54,979 --> 00:22:58,357
We can tell the police that you didn't
know what was in the casket because

363
00:22:58,440 --> 00:22:59,441
you really didn't know, right?

364
00:22:59,525 --> 00:23:01,777
No, Heeju.
Wait, wait, wait, Heeju.

365
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:04,071
Wait a minute.
Wait a minute.

366
00:23:05,489 --> 00:23:10,911
[Dokyung] So you're completely sure no one
knows that you hid the van in the mines?

367
00:23:19,670 --> 00:23:20,963
[bus engine rumbling]

368
00:23:21,046 --> 00:23:23,841
JEONGSAN BUS TERMINAL

369
00:23:23,924 --> 00:23:26,885
[♪ tense music]

370
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:32,641
[Dokyung] Heeju.

371
00:23:34,393 --> 00:23:36,270
Don't tell anyone where the casket is.

372
00:23:37,479 --> 00:23:39,023
No one but the two of us can know.

373
00:23:40,107 --> 00:23:41,859
I won't tell anyone, either.

374
00:23:43,444 --> 00:23:45,237
I swear I'll keep it a secret.

375
00:23:46,155 --> 00:23:47,197
No matter what.

376
00:23:48,574 --> 00:23:50,492
Even with a knife to my throat.

377
00:23:53,328 --> 00:23:54,747
[bus engine rumbling]

378
00:23:54,830 --> 00:23:56,248
[brakes hissing]

379
00:24:02,004 --> 00:24:04,965
[bus engine revving]

380
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:09,803
[birds chirping]

381
00:24:11,930 --> 00:24:15,309
[Dokyung] From now on,
this is our whole lives.

382
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:21,148
[Dokyung] I'm gonna turn myself in.

383
00:24:22,399 --> 00:24:24,318
If the police can't find the gold bars...

384
00:24:25,611 --> 00:24:26,612
...I could get out in a year.

385
00:24:27,780 --> 00:24:30,741
[Dokyung] With a good lawyer I could
even get a suspended sentence.

386
00:24:31,784 --> 00:24:34,244
You're gonna have to keep
the gold safe for us, Heeju.

387
00:24:35,037 --> 00:24:36,371
Until I can get out.
STYLE
::cue()

388
00:24:37,498 --> 00:24:40,501
[Heeju breathing heavily]

389
00:24:46,882 --> 00:24:48,050
[groans]

390
00:24:49,134 --> 00:24:51,178
[exhales sharply]

391
00:24:51,261 --> 00:24:52,262
[grunts]

392
00:25:03,232 --> 00:25:05,025
[breathing heavily]

393
00:25:11,698 --> 00:25:13,325
[exhales]

394
00:25:13,408 --> 00:25:18,205
DAD! BE SAFE AGAIN TODAY

395
00:25:18,288 --> 00:25:19,540
[car trunk opening]

396
00:25:21,750 --> 00:25:22,918
[exhales]

397
00:25:29,383 --> 00:25:31,760
[Dokyung] First, bury the gold bars
in the mine...

398
00:25:32,594 --> 00:25:34,721
...so that if anyone goes in,
they won't see them.

399
00:25:36,140 --> 00:25:37,724
[zipper unzipping]

400
00:25:37,808 --> 00:25:39,017
[water dripping]

401
00:25:45,357 --> 00:25:46,650
Move them one at a time.

402
00:25:46,733 --> 00:25:48,152
I know you can do it.

403
00:25:49,153 --> 00:25:50,320
[Dokyung] It will take a while.

404
00:25:50,404 --> 00:25:52,072
[grunts]

405
00:25:52,156 --> 00:25:53,574
[Dokyung] But please bury them.

406
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:03,041
[gold bar clinks]

407
00:26:03,125 --> 00:26:04,126
[Heeju grunts]

408
00:26:05,627 --> 00:26:08,630
[grunting]

409
00:26:11,967 --> 00:26:15,512
[water dripping continues]

410
00:26:15,596 --> 00:26:17,347
[gold bar clangs]
[Heeju groans]

411
00:26:26,148 --> 00:26:27,149
[lighter flicks]

412
00:27:06,939 --> 00:27:09,316
[Dokyung] Take the van back
to the abandoned warehouse.

413
00:27:09,399 --> 00:27:10,692
The one from that night.

414
00:27:16,657 --> 00:27:17,991
[bottle spritzing]

415
00:27:19,368 --> 00:27:21,745
[Dokyung] Make sure you don't
leave fingerprints or anything.

416
00:27:23,038 --> 00:27:27,000
That way even if the police find the van,
it won't matter.

417
00:27:27,960 --> 00:27:29,211
They can't trace it to you.

418
00:27:38,595 --> 00:27:40,472
[Dokyung] Find a place
to lay low for a while.

419
00:27:41,682 --> 00:27:42,808
Don't try to contact me.

420
00:27:43,558 --> 00:27:44,810
Don't even look for me.

421
00:27:46,770 --> 00:27:51,066
[Dokyung] I will find a way
to contact you if it's necessary.

422
00:28:16,216 --> 00:28:18,093
[Hocheol] Hey, Captain.
STYLE
::cue()

423
00:28:19,219 --> 00:28:21,179
It's me, Park.

424
00:28:25,267 --> 00:28:27,477
[metal chair clanking]

425
00:28:29,396 --> 00:28:31,565
[Hocheol] Ah, open your eyes.

426
00:28:32,315 --> 00:28:33,608
I know you're awake.

427
00:28:35,944 --> 00:28:37,654
[wincing]

428
00:28:37,738 --> 00:28:39,448
[panicked breathing]

429
00:28:40,407 --> 00:28:42,325
You look like you're gonna piss yourself.

430
00:28:47,039 --> 00:28:49,374
How did a little bitch
like you pull this off?

431
00:28:49,458 --> 00:28:50,667
[Hocheol] Why'd you do it?

432
00:28:51,835 --> 00:28:55,297
You upset?
Did I somehow upset you?

433
00:28:55,380 --> 00:28:58,759
[Hocheol] Up until now,
we always got along.

434
00:28:58,842 --> 00:29:00,886
You that desperate for cash?

435
00:29:02,345 --> 00:29:04,139
[Hocheol] Money always screws things up.

436
00:29:04,222 --> 00:29:05,515
I understand.

437
00:29:07,559 --> 00:29:10,103
Well, I guess I'm
the one who put you here,

438
00:29:10,187 --> 00:29:11,938
so I'm partly to blame.

439
00:29:13,398 --> 00:29:16,068
[Hocheol] Let's go back
to the original deal.

440
00:29:16,151 --> 00:29:18,987
The casket for 200 million.

441
00:29:19,696 --> 00:29:22,616
Ah, it's fine.
You don't need to say anything.

442
00:29:22,699 --> 00:29:24,493
[panicked breathing]

443
00:29:25,410 --> 00:29:26,661
[Hocheol] This is your phone, right?

444
00:29:29,998 --> 00:29:31,583
[Hocheol] Your partner,
the one who took off with the van?

445
00:29:32,375 --> 00:29:33,418
Call him.

446
00:29:34,461 --> 00:29:36,838
Found his burner phone.
The real one.

447
00:29:38,131 --> 00:29:39,132
Now, which is it?

448
00:29:41,176 --> 00:29:42,177
[Hocheol] Huh?

449
00:29:43,178 --> 00:29:45,597
All you need is a finger.
Just press it, you little...

450
00:29:45,680 --> 00:29:47,140
You really expect me to trust you?

451
00:29:48,725 --> 00:29:50,977
You might kill me after I return
the casket.

452
00:29:52,729 --> 00:29:53,980
[Dokyung] You already tried to
kill me once.

453
00:29:56,608 --> 00:29:58,068
[Hocheol] Yeah, I know.

454
00:29:59,236 --> 00:30:01,196
Why did I do that?

455
00:30:01,279 --> 00:30:02,739
Deposit one billion won into my account.

456
00:30:03,907 --> 00:30:05,075
Get all these cops off my tail.

457
00:30:06,076 --> 00:30:07,536
And get me out of the country.

458
00:30:09,913 --> 00:30:11,623
Then I'll tell you where the casket is.

459
00:30:11,706 --> 00:30:13,750
Like I can trust you.

460
00:30:13,834 --> 00:30:15,168
[exhales sharply]

461
00:30:16,086 --> 00:30:18,213
I've got nothin' to tell you, then.

462
00:30:19,172 --> 00:30:20,465
Okay.

463
00:30:22,676 --> 00:30:24,344
[Hocheol] Heard you got 22 stitches.

464
00:30:25,262 --> 00:30:26,263
[Hocheol] Let's open 'em up!

465
00:30:26,346 --> 00:30:28,098
[muffled shouting]

466
00:30:28,181 --> 00:30:31,309
Just one fucking phone call
and this'd be over.

467
00:30:31,393 --> 00:30:34,771
You should have called when I
was being nice, you stupid fuck!

468
00:30:34,855 --> 00:30:36,148
[groaning]

469
00:30:36,231 --> 00:30:37,899
-[grunting]
-[Detective Kang] Sir!

470
00:30:39,484 --> 00:30:41,236
[muffled groaning]

471
00:30:41,319 --> 00:30:43,572
[breathing heavily]

472
00:30:45,240 --> 00:30:46,867
Better take care of yourself.

473
00:30:48,368 --> 00:30:50,328
I'll be back soon, Captain.

474
00:30:50,412 --> 00:30:53,456
[breathing heavily]

475
00:30:53,540 --> 00:30:56,543
[crickets chirping]

476
00:31:16,146 --> 00:31:22,152
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

477
00:31:30,911 --> 00:31:32,787
[door squeaking]

478
00:31:35,248 --> 00:31:36,708
[Sunok] We're closed.

479
00:31:41,296 --> 00:31:42,756
[Sunok] What's going on?

480
00:31:42,839 --> 00:31:44,633
What are you doing here?

481
00:31:48,220 --> 00:31:50,472
I'm just gonna stay here for a little.

482
00:31:50,555 --> 00:31:51,973
A few days.

483
00:31:52,057 --> 00:31:54,935
Well, maybe a month.

484
00:31:55,018 --> 00:31:56,561
What about work?

485
00:31:57,479 --> 00:32:01,524
I quit, so it'll only be until
I find something else.
STYLE
::cue()

486
00:32:01,608 --> 00:32:03,068
Don't worry. It won't be long.

487
00:32:03,151 --> 00:32:05,195
You said you'd never come back.

488
00:32:06,863 --> 00:32:09,532
[Sunok] Guess you found out the real world
isn't so easy, huh?

489
00:32:10,533 --> 00:32:11,993
[Sunok scoffs]

490
00:32:12,077 --> 00:32:15,413
That's what life is like for women
with nothing to offer but their body.

491
00:32:15,497 --> 00:32:18,458
I didn't live like you did, Auntie.

492
00:32:18,541 --> 00:32:19,542
Then why'd you crawl back here?

493
00:32:20,627 --> 00:32:22,963
You say it's temporary but you can't
even afford a hotel?

494
00:32:23,046 --> 00:32:24,214
And what about you?

495
00:32:24,297 --> 00:32:25,924
Are you still living with
a man who beats you?

496
00:32:28,301 --> 00:32:29,928
[exhales]

497
00:32:30,011 --> 00:32:32,222
Forget it.
I'll get a hotel.

498
00:32:32,722 --> 00:32:34,557
[Sunok] If it's really only
for a little while,

499
00:32:34,641 --> 00:32:36,685
you can stay here.

500
00:32:40,814 --> 00:32:42,065
I said you can stay.

501
00:32:46,444 --> 00:32:47,696
Have you eaten?

502
00:32:48,655 --> 00:32:50,907
It's fine.
I'll take care of myself.

503
00:32:51,741 --> 00:32:53,410
I'll just come back here to sleep.

504
00:32:55,120 --> 00:32:58,290
Is that, uh, gambling den still here?

505
00:33:00,250 --> 00:33:02,210
Nope. We had to stop.

506
00:33:03,336 --> 00:33:05,088
We got raided, so...

507
00:33:05,171 --> 00:33:08,717
-Then what is he up to now?
-I don't know.

508
00:33:09,718 --> 00:33:10,802
He barely comes home these days.

509
00:33:12,012 --> 00:33:13,305
That's a good thing.

510
00:33:14,306 --> 00:33:15,682
I don't want him to know I'm here.

511
00:33:15,765 --> 00:33:17,183
Don't tell anyone else, either.

512
00:33:17,267 --> 00:33:19,728
No one around here
is asking about you.

513
00:33:20,687 --> 00:33:21,688
Where are you going?

514
00:33:22,439 --> 00:33:24,107
I'm getting sheets for you.

515
00:33:24,190 --> 00:33:25,775
You're gonna have to sleep in the vault.

516
00:33:25,859 --> 00:33:29,487
[Sunok] The latch is broken,
so make sure you lock the front door.

517
00:33:30,572 --> 00:33:32,449
[Sunok] Oh, look at you.

518
00:33:34,117 --> 00:33:35,785
[Sunok] The bags under your eyes
look awful.

519
00:33:35,869 --> 00:33:37,120
And what's on your hands?

520
00:33:39,706 --> 00:33:40,665
What the hell have you been doing?

521
00:33:43,126 --> 00:33:45,337
Oh, forget it.

522
00:33:52,677 --> 00:33:53,762
[sink turns on]

523
00:33:53,845 --> 00:33:57,182
[water running]

524
00:34:08,902 --> 00:34:10,028
[exhales sharply]

525
00:34:12,197 --> 00:34:14,699
[Dokyung] When this goes to court,
I'll need an expensive lawyer.

526
00:34:15,241 --> 00:34:16,493
And money for bail.

527
00:34:16,576 --> 00:34:18,244
GOLD BAR

528
00:34:18,328 --> 00:34:21,456
We can sell one gold bar
and use that to cover expenses.

529
00:34:22,749 --> 00:34:24,376
Okay, how?

530
00:34:25,835 --> 00:34:28,296
There must be a way to do it.

531
00:34:28,380 --> 00:34:30,173
[Dokyung] See what you can find out.
I'll look into it, too.

532
00:34:30,256 --> 00:34:31,132
HOW TO BUY AND SELL
A 75-GRAM GOLD BAR?

533
00:34:31,216 --> 00:34:32,133
WHAT IS A 75-GRAM GOLD BAR?

534
00:34:41,810 --> 00:34:42,852
[Dokyung] Heeju.

535
00:34:43,895 --> 00:34:45,730
When I get out of prison,

536
00:34:45,814 --> 00:34:49,401
the first thing we'll do is sell all
the gold bars and get outta here.

537
00:34:50,735 --> 00:34:52,570
Maybe France or wherever.

538
00:34:53,613 --> 00:34:54,864
[Dokyung] Somewhere no one
will ever find us.

539
00:34:56,533 --> 00:34:59,244
This is a once in a lifetime opportunity
for us, Heeju.

540
00:35:00,286 --> 00:35:02,706
It could completely change our lives.

541
00:35:02,789 --> 00:35:04,040
You can do this.

542
00:35:13,633 --> 00:35:14,926
[gold bar clinks]

543
00:35:19,389 --> 00:35:22,392
[♪ suspenseful music]
STYLE
::cue()

544
00:35:41,035 --> 00:35:42,912
[Investigating Officer A]
Have you ever seen this van before, sir?

545
00:35:44,372 --> 00:35:45,707
No, I've never seen it before.

546
00:35:45,790 --> 00:35:47,292
There's no van like that
in the neighborhood,

547
00:35:47,375 --> 00:35:48,543
so I have no idea how it got there.

548
00:35:48,626 --> 00:35:50,462
[Investigating Officer A]
Do you have any injuries?

549
00:35:50,545 --> 00:35:51,838
[Witness] I mean, I'm not hurt anywhere.

550
00:35:51,921 --> 00:35:53,173
But look at this.

551
00:35:53,256 --> 00:35:55,717
When I got here,
everything was a mess.

552
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:58,094
It looks like someone crashed
and left the van here.

553
00:35:58,178 --> 00:36:01,973
We found the van, sir,
with the 9900 plate.

554
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:04,851
[Investigating Officer B] Casket?
There's no casket here.

555
00:36:05,810 --> 00:36:08,438
-What do you wanna eat?
-I dunno.

556
00:36:08,521 --> 00:36:09,814
Ah, shit.
[phone beeps]

557
00:36:09,898 --> 00:36:11,858
[Male Detective A] I'm starving.

558
00:36:11,941 --> 00:36:14,986
They found the van,
but the casket's not in there.

559
00:36:15,069 --> 00:36:17,614
Lee Dokyung keeps denying
that he knows anything about it.

560
00:36:17,697 --> 00:36:19,741
-For now, at least.
-[Hocheol] Good work.

561
00:36:20,950 --> 00:36:22,869
Come to the hotel soon.
We'll grab food.

562
00:36:26,289 --> 00:36:27,290
[phone beeps]

563
00:36:27,373 --> 00:36:29,459
[inhales]

564
00:36:31,544 --> 00:36:35,381
All the men we sent to the airport,
you picked them out yourself, right?

565
00:36:35,465 --> 00:36:36,925
Yeah.

566
00:36:37,008 --> 00:36:39,511
You specifically told me to pick out
the smartest and strongest.

567
00:36:40,512 --> 00:36:42,263
Lee Dokyung didn't act on his own.

568
00:36:42,347 --> 00:36:44,516
[exhales]
There's someone else.

569
00:36:44,599 --> 00:36:46,392
Ah!

570
00:36:46,476 --> 00:36:49,312
I already told you,
it's not one of my boys!

571
00:36:49,395 --> 00:36:51,356
[Gitae] I think...
[door opens]

572
00:36:53,483 --> 00:36:54,526
You wanted to see me?

573
00:36:56,611 --> 00:36:58,238
[Hocheol inhales on cigarette]

574
00:37:00,698 --> 00:37:03,117
Hand over your phone.
You gotta unlock it.

575
00:37:13,419 --> 00:37:14,879
[Hocheol] Where'd you hide the casket?

576
00:37:15,964 --> 00:37:17,006
What?

577
00:37:17,090 --> 00:37:19,676
You were the one who drove the van
from Yangpo Airport.

578
00:37:19,759 --> 00:37:22,846
Uh, I already told my boss all about it.

579
00:37:24,305 --> 00:37:25,974
That shit head pilot.

580
00:37:26,891 --> 00:37:28,893
Uh, Lee Dokyung, he...

581
00:37:29,519 --> 00:37:31,855
...he pulled out a gun
and held it to my head.

582
00:37:32,564 --> 00:37:34,190
He took off with the van.

583
00:37:34,274 --> 00:37:38,820
But that night, the first person
to find our missing van was you.

584
00:37:39,571 --> 00:37:40,572
You.

585
00:37:40,655 --> 00:37:43,867
[Hocheol] And you were the only one
who saw the driver's face.

586
00:37:43,950 --> 00:37:46,411
Aren't you gonna tell me who it was?

587
00:37:47,370 --> 00:37:50,248
Uh, yeah, I mean...

588
00:37:51,624 --> 00:37:53,918
I did my best to try and get
a good look.

589
00:37:54,002 --> 00:37:55,461
It-it was just so dark, though.

590
00:37:55,545 --> 00:37:56,671
Yeah, and the casket?

591
00:37:57,338 --> 00:37:58,339
[Woogy] Sir.

592
00:37:58,423 --> 00:38:00,925
I don't know.
I-I swear it wasn't me.

593
00:38:01,009 --> 00:38:04,387
I-I passed out yesterday 'cause I
was all beat up.

594
00:38:06,264 --> 00:38:08,182
[phone clatters on floor]

595
00:38:10,727 --> 00:38:13,354
-[grunts]
-[pained groaning]

596
00:38:13,438 --> 00:38:15,773
Hey, boss. This isn't right.

597
00:38:15,857 --> 00:38:17,650
Get your fucking hands off.

598
00:38:18,526 --> 00:38:21,029
-[grunts]
-[Woogy groaning]

599
00:38:23,573 --> 00:38:26,910
I already know everything
so either confess or lose an ear.

600
00:38:26,993 --> 00:38:29,412
Sir, I dunno. I promise.

601
00:38:29,495 --> 00:38:31,331
I'm telling the truth.
I swear I'm telling you...

602
00:38:31,414 --> 00:38:32,832
Lee Dokyung already told the police
you helped him,

603
00:38:32,916 --> 00:38:33,875
so just tell me where it is!

604
00:38:33,958 --> 00:38:35,335
[Woogy whimpers]

605
00:38:35,418 --> 00:38:38,004
[Hocheol] This is your last chance
to confess, you asshole!

606
00:38:38,087 --> 00:38:39,672
[Gitae] You serious?

607
00:38:39,756 --> 00:38:41,591
Woogy, you shit.
You tell him where it is now!

608
00:38:41,674 --> 00:38:43,593
No, I don't know anything! Ah!

609
00:38:43,676 --> 00:38:45,011
[Woogy shouting]

610
00:38:45,094 --> 00:38:48,264
Please don't kill me! Please!

611
00:38:48,348 --> 00:38:49,349
[grunts]

612
00:38:49,432 --> 00:38:51,601
[Woogy whimpering]

613
00:38:54,062 --> 00:38:55,605
Get the fuck out of my sight.

614
00:38:55,688 --> 00:38:58,191
-[whimpering]
-[Hocheol] Fuck!

615
00:38:59,567 --> 00:39:01,361
[kicks phone]

616
00:39:03,780 --> 00:39:06,032
[groans]

617
00:39:06,115 --> 00:39:07,200
[Woogy] I'll get going, sir.
STYLE
::cue()

618
00:39:09,369 --> 00:39:10,828
[exhales sharply]

619
00:39:14,582 --> 00:39:15,750
[door closes]

620
00:39:17,043 --> 00:39:18,836
[Gitae] It's not him?

621
00:39:18,920 --> 00:39:21,756
Well, what the hell was that all about,
then?

622
00:39:21,839 --> 00:39:25,718
Lee Dokyung did have an accomplice,
and that person hid the casket.

623
00:39:26,761 --> 00:39:29,305
I had to make sure that
it wasn't one of our guys.

624
00:39:29,389 --> 00:39:31,265
[exhales sharply]
What are you gonna do?

625
00:39:31,349 --> 00:39:32,558
[Hocheol scoffs]

626
00:39:32,642 --> 00:39:35,061
Seems like finding the casket
isn't even our biggest problem.

627
00:39:36,229 --> 00:39:37,397
[exhales sharply]

628
00:39:38,481 --> 00:39:39,899
Does the chairman know?

629
00:39:41,067 --> 00:39:42,777
[exhales]

630
00:39:44,028 --> 00:39:45,238
[sighs]

631
00:39:45,321 --> 00:39:47,782
-I'm sorry.
-[exhales]

632
00:39:47,865 --> 00:39:49,367
Must be really tough on you.

633
00:39:49,450 --> 00:39:53,621
[Gitae] Didn't he say once he wraps up
in Cambodia and returns to Gold Land,

634
00:39:53,705 --> 00:39:55,331
he'd hand over the hotel
and everything else to you?

635
00:39:55,415 --> 00:39:58,376
[Gitae] You really should do your best not
to upset him right now.

636
00:39:58,459 --> 00:39:59,836
[Hocheol] Fucker!

637
00:39:59,919 --> 00:40:01,838
You need to shut it.

638
00:40:03,006 --> 00:40:04,048
[exhales angrily]

639
00:40:09,053 --> 00:40:10,805
You can murder just about anyone.

640
00:40:12,140 --> 00:40:14,642
The chairman will forgive you for that,
but if you lose his money...

641
00:40:15,435 --> 00:40:16,644
That's a different story.

642
00:40:18,021 --> 00:40:19,188
[Gitae] What are you gonna do?

643
00:40:20,023 --> 00:40:21,441
[Gitae] He'll be coming back soon.

644
00:40:48,342 --> 00:40:50,636
[locker doors banging]

645
00:40:50,720 --> 00:40:52,305
[pills rattling]

646
00:41:09,197 --> 00:41:12,200
[wound squelches]

647
00:41:34,263 --> 00:41:36,849
[door creaks open]

648
00:41:36,933 --> 00:41:38,518
Come on in.

649
00:41:41,979 --> 00:41:43,397
Hmm.

650
00:41:45,650 --> 00:41:46,943
Are you here to sell?

651
00:41:48,778 --> 00:41:51,739
Oh. I'm guessing you don't recognize me.

652
00:41:51,823 --> 00:41:55,284
[Woogy] I used to live in Bukju, too.
The old mining town there.

653
00:41:57,578 --> 00:41:58,579
No?

654
00:41:59,539 --> 00:42:00,832
Really?

655
00:42:00,915 --> 00:42:03,459
[Woogy] Everyone tells me I look
just like when I was a kid.

656
00:42:04,418 --> 00:42:06,420
[Woogy exhales sharply]
I guess you don't remember.

657
00:42:07,588 --> 00:42:08,881
[Woogy] So, tell me.

658
00:42:09,841 --> 00:42:11,092
Is Heeju with you?

659
00:42:11,175 --> 00:42:14,387
[Woogy] I heard she went to Seoul
a while ago, but is she back now?

660
00:42:14,470 --> 00:42:16,013
She's not.

661
00:42:16,097 --> 00:42:19,267
Oh, she's not? Hmm.
Thought I saw her.

662
00:42:19,350 --> 00:42:20,852
[laughs]

663
00:42:20,935 --> 00:42:22,270
Heeju's not here.

664
00:42:22,353 --> 00:42:23,771
I doubt she's ever coming back.

665
00:42:24,939 --> 00:42:26,023
[Sunok] So pawn something or get out.

666
00:42:28,442 --> 00:42:31,279
Yeah, sure. Got a business to run.
[chuckles]

667
00:42:31,362 --> 00:42:32,738
[Woogy exhales]

668
00:42:33,364 --> 00:42:34,365
[Woogy] See ya!

669
00:42:34,448 --> 00:42:36,409
[door creaks shut]
STYLE
::cue()

670
00:42:36,492 --> 00:42:38,119
[truck engine rumbling]

671
00:42:47,879 --> 00:42:50,006
DONGHWA JEWELRY

672
00:42:50,089 --> 00:42:52,758
[Male Jewelry Store Owner]
Did you say a 10-kilogram gold bar?

673
00:42:52,842 --> 00:42:54,760
Uh, I don't really have anything that big.

674
00:42:54,844 --> 00:42:56,345
There's not really a market for that.

675
00:42:56,429 --> 00:42:57,972
[Male Jewelry Store Owner]
I mean, I guess if someone

676
00:42:58,055 --> 00:43:01,350
really wanted one,
it could be made to order, but...

677
00:43:01,434 --> 00:43:03,394
-How much would it cost?
-[Male Jewelry Store Owner] Right now?

678
00:43:03,477 --> 00:43:06,189
With our economy the way it is,
the current price of gold is pretty high.

679
00:43:06,272 --> 00:43:08,774
[Male Jewelry Store Owner]
A kilo could go up to 150 million,

680
00:43:08,858 --> 00:43:12,445
so ten kilos is 1.5 billion.

681
00:43:12,528 --> 00:43:13,446
[inhales sharply]

682
00:43:13,529 --> 00:43:14,488
Mm.

683
00:43:14,572 --> 00:43:17,074
So, how much...

684
00:43:18,242 --> 00:43:20,995
...do you think someone would be able
to sell it for?

685
00:43:22,622 --> 00:43:25,625
Well, first I gotta make sure
it's pure gold.

686
00:43:25,708 --> 00:43:27,168
So I'd need to get a look at it.

687
00:43:27,251 --> 00:43:31,964
If it is pure, then I'd consider
offering 1.3 or 4 billion.

688
00:43:32,048 --> 00:43:34,967
I know, market price is higher than that.

689
00:43:35,051 --> 00:43:37,678
[Male Jewelry Store Owner]
Are you saying you have a 10-kilogram bar

690
00:43:37,762 --> 00:43:39,430
of pure gold you're looking to sell?

691
00:43:39,513 --> 00:43:41,849
Uh, no, I don't.

692
00:43:43,559 --> 00:43:44,936
Just curious.

693
00:43:45,019 --> 00:43:46,479
Just go.

694
00:43:47,855 --> 00:43:49,065
You're wasting my time, young lady.

695
00:44:24,433 --> 00:44:28,771
BEER, LIQUOR, MIJA

696
00:44:28,854 --> 00:44:29,939
[rustling]

697
00:44:30,022 --> 00:44:31,023
Who is it?

698
00:44:31,774 --> 00:44:32,942
[grunts]

699
00:44:33,025 --> 00:44:34,944
Hold on.
I haven't even opened yet.

700
00:44:35,027 --> 00:44:36,112
[grunts]

701
00:44:37,613 --> 00:44:39,031
[Mija] Heeju?

702
00:44:39,115 --> 00:44:41,158
Wh-what are you doing here?

703
00:44:41,242 --> 00:44:42,535
[chuckles]

704
00:44:42,618 --> 00:44:43,869
Auntie, how are you?

705
00:44:43,953 --> 00:44:46,664
Oh, same old, same old!

706
00:44:46,747 --> 00:44:48,874
This way. Oh!

707
00:44:48,958 --> 00:44:50,876
[Mija] Look at you. Sit down!

708
00:44:50,960 --> 00:44:53,337
[chuckles]

709
00:44:53,421 --> 00:44:55,381
Excuse the mess.
I was just eating.

710
00:44:55,464 --> 00:44:56,716
Have you eaten yet?

711
00:44:56,799 --> 00:44:57,800
Yeah.

712
00:44:59,260 --> 00:45:00,678
Oh, it's been so long.

713
00:45:01,637 --> 00:45:03,264
When'd you come back?
You here to stay?

714
00:45:03,347 --> 00:45:05,474
No, just here a little while.

715
00:45:05,558 --> 00:45:06,767
[Mija] You brat.

716
00:45:06,851 --> 00:45:08,853
You never even called me once.

717
00:45:08,936 --> 00:45:10,438
I'm sorry, Auntie.

718
00:45:10,521 --> 00:45:12,815
I was busy trying to make a living.

719
00:45:12,898 --> 00:45:13,899
Yeah, of course you were.

720
00:45:15,192 --> 00:45:16,402
[sniffles]

721
00:45:16,485 --> 00:45:17,737
So how are you really doing?

722
00:45:19,322 --> 00:45:20,489
Well...

723
00:45:22,408 --> 00:45:23,409
...would you...

724
00:45:24,368 --> 00:45:28,164
...could you maybe lend me some money?

725
00:45:29,165 --> 00:45:30,207
How much you need?

726
00:45:32,460 --> 00:45:35,671
It's kind of a lot.
50 million won or so.

727
00:45:37,173 --> 00:45:39,300
I could pay it back really quickly,
though.

728
00:45:39,383 --> 00:45:40,509
I'll have it in a month or so.

729
00:45:40,593 --> 00:45:42,887
[Mija] Things haven't been easy for you,
either, have they?

730
00:45:42,970 --> 00:45:44,805
[whimpers]

731
00:45:46,599 --> 00:45:48,642
Of course you need money.

732
00:45:50,019 --> 00:45:51,854
Sunok's cancer,
I know all about it.

733
00:45:53,814 --> 00:45:57,151
[Mija] I mean, I tried to get her
to go to the hospital, but she won't go.

734
00:45:57,234 --> 00:45:59,695
She said she can barely afford food
for herself.

735
00:46:00,738 --> 00:46:02,156
[Mija] I don't even think
your uncle knows.

736
00:46:02,239 --> 00:46:04,158
Not that he'd care.

737
00:46:04,700 --> 00:46:08,079
Shit, he barely treats her like a person.

738
00:46:08,162 --> 00:46:10,122
Oh, it pisses me off.

739
00:46:10,206 --> 00:46:11,832
[crying]

740
00:46:12,792 --> 00:46:13,959
I know.

741
00:46:14,877 --> 00:46:18,422
I know all her medical bills would be
about 50 million won.

742
00:46:19,673 --> 00:46:21,967
[Mija] Hospital, treatments, operation.

743
00:46:22,718 --> 00:46:23,719
[Mija exhales]

744
00:46:23,803 --> 00:46:24,887
[Mija sniffles]

745
00:46:26,305 --> 00:46:27,390
[Mija] I don't have that kind of money.

746
00:46:29,350 --> 00:46:31,227
I live paycheck to paycheck, too.

747
00:46:31,310 --> 00:46:32,603
I've got nothing.

748
00:46:40,277 --> 00:46:41,278
[exhales]

749
00:46:46,200 --> 00:46:47,910
-[Woogy] Hey, Heeju!
-[gasps]

750
00:46:50,204 --> 00:46:51,205
Is that you?

751
00:46:52,248 --> 00:46:54,333
[Woogy laughs]
It is you!

752
00:46:54,417 --> 00:46:56,043
Long time, no see!

753
00:46:56,127 --> 00:46:58,170
It's me, Woogy.

754
00:46:59,964 --> 00:47:02,383
We both lived in that mining town
when we were kids.

755
00:47:02,466 --> 00:47:05,469
Sorry, I don't really...

756
00:47:05,553 --> 00:47:07,638
Sure you do. I was the kid with
the bald spot right here.

757
00:47:09,515 --> 00:47:11,308
What'cha doin'?

758
00:47:11,392 --> 00:47:13,561
[Woogy] You buyin' somethin'?
A ring?

759
00:47:14,478 --> 00:47:15,563
I can get you a good deal.

760
00:47:19,024 --> 00:47:21,569
Ah, damn.
It's been so long, right?

761
00:47:22,903 --> 00:47:26,615
We went to, uh, elementary school together
so it's been...

762
00:47:27,491 --> 00:47:28,826
...over ten years now?
STYLE
::cue()

763
00:47:28,909 --> 00:47:29,994
[exhales sharply]

764
00:47:31,328 --> 00:47:32,580
Okay, how 'bout Chan?

765
00:47:33,330 --> 00:47:36,041
Or Seonghun? You know, the kid who
followed you 'cause he liked you.

766
00:47:36,876 --> 00:47:38,377
No, I don't.

767
00:47:39,295 --> 00:47:41,005
Sorry, I don't remember.

768
00:47:49,555 --> 00:47:51,182
Well, that hurt my feelings a little.

769
00:47:51,932 --> 00:47:54,685
Hey, you really don't remember?

770
00:47:55,144 --> 00:47:56,270
'Cause I remember you.

771
00:47:58,522 --> 00:47:59,982
Wait, wait!
What about freeze tag?

772
00:48:00,065 --> 00:48:02,067
We used to always play
after school together.

773
00:48:02,151 --> 00:48:03,777
I'd get tagged and you'd unfreeze me.

774
00:48:04,445 --> 00:48:07,156
Maybe this'll jog your memory!
Freeze!

775
00:48:07,239 --> 00:48:08,908
[exhales sharply]

776
00:48:12,578 --> 00:48:15,956
[breathing heavily]

777
00:48:16,040 --> 00:48:17,750
[Heeju wails]

778
00:48:17,833 --> 00:48:19,168
[bus door squeaks]

779
00:48:22,254 --> 00:48:23,672
[exhales sharply]

780
00:48:32,431 --> 00:48:33,432
[knocking]

781
00:48:33,516 --> 00:48:35,142
[gasps]

782
00:48:35,226 --> 00:48:36,727
I'll see you around!

783
00:48:47,780 --> 00:48:50,783
[whimpers]

784
00:48:54,537 --> 00:48:55,871
[glass cracking]

785
00:48:56,580 --> 00:48:57,790
[screams]

786
00:48:57,873 --> 00:48:59,625
[panicked breathing]

787
00:48:59,708 --> 00:49:00,918
[Heeju screams]

788
00:49:05,965 --> 00:49:08,801
[breathing heavily]

789
00:49:11,845 --> 00:49:14,265
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

790
00:49:15,057 --> 00:49:17,935
[Mr. Jang grunts]

791
00:49:18,018 --> 00:49:21,230
'Kay, let me see.

792
00:49:21,605 --> 00:49:23,774
[inhales sharply]

793
00:49:23,857 --> 00:49:25,276
[groans]

794
00:49:25,359 --> 00:49:27,570
[Mr. Jang] Yeah, this is real.

795
00:49:29,029 --> 00:49:31,407
How-how much you give for it?

796
00:49:31,490 --> 00:49:32,741
You don't need to know that.

797
00:49:34,034 --> 00:49:35,578
And they never came back for it?

798
00:49:35,661 --> 00:49:37,037
It's been over three months.

799
00:49:37,121 --> 00:49:40,082
It's been over three months. Hmm.

800
00:49:43,669 --> 00:49:45,504
[Mr. Jang] I'll give you 25 million.

801
00:49:45,588 --> 00:49:48,173
-We'll say 30 mill on the receipt, though.
-[Sunok] Mr. Jang.

802
00:49:48,257 --> 00:49:51,552
All these years we've been doing business
and that's the best you can do?

803
00:49:52,511 --> 00:49:54,179
I'm being generous here.

804
00:49:54,263 --> 00:49:55,556
Collateral isn't worth market price.

805
00:49:55,639 --> 00:49:57,141
Just pay for the gold ring and get out.

806
00:49:57,224 --> 00:49:58,350
I can find someone else
on my own for this.

807
00:49:58,434 --> 00:49:59,393
[Mr. Jang] All right, all right!

808
00:49:59,476 --> 00:50:01,186
All right.
All right, all right.

809
00:50:01,270 --> 00:50:02,688
I'll do it.

810
00:50:02,771 --> 00:50:04,231
[Mr. Jang] I'll give you 27.

811
00:50:04,315 --> 00:50:06,025
[inhales deeply]

812
00:50:06,108 --> 00:50:08,235
You understand I need
to make money, too.

813
00:50:08,319 --> 00:50:09,862
30 million.

814
00:50:09,945 --> 00:50:11,739
[inhales]

815
00:50:11,822 --> 00:50:13,365
Someone else already offered me 35.

816
00:50:13,449 --> 00:50:15,659
Okay, all right.
I'll pay you tomorrow.

817
00:50:17,161 --> 00:50:18,162
You drive a hard bargain.

818
00:50:23,083 --> 00:50:26,962
[groaning]

819
00:50:28,589 --> 00:50:30,341
Ah, shit.

820
00:50:31,425 --> 00:50:33,052
Fucking bitch.

821
00:50:33,552 --> 00:50:35,429
[snorts, spits]

822
00:50:37,222 --> 00:50:38,641
[humming]

823
00:50:39,683 --> 00:50:41,518
Mr. Jang, wait.

824
00:50:42,436 --> 00:50:43,562
Who are you?

825
00:50:45,314 --> 00:50:48,359
I heard you trade in gold.
Do you?

826
00:50:48,901 --> 00:50:50,402
[Mr. Jang] Yeah, I do.

827
00:50:50,486 --> 00:50:51,862
Which pawn shop are you with?

828
00:50:52,738 --> 00:50:54,657
Don't think we've met yet.

829
00:50:54,740 --> 00:50:57,534
If the piece is really big,
would you still buy it?

830
00:50:57,618 --> 00:51:00,329
Cast gold,
or something like a golden pig?

831
00:51:00,412 --> 00:51:01,580
[inhales]

832
00:51:02,539 --> 00:51:03,916
A bar. A gold bar.

833
00:51:03,999 --> 00:51:06,001
A gold bar?

834
00:51:07,211 --> 00:51:09,713
Is it pure? How heavy?

835
00:51:12,257 --> 00:51:13,592
Ten?

836
00:51:14,259 --> 00:51:15,260
I'll buy it.

837
00:51:16,178 --> 00:51:17,388
[Mr. Jang] I'd need to see it.

838
00:51:19,890 --> 00:51:21,975
How 'bout you get in the car.
Show me and we'll talk.

839
00:51:22,059 --> 00:51:23,060
No.

840
00:51:23,143 --> 00:51:27,690
Uh, could you just give me
an estimate, please?

841
00:51:28,357 --> 00:51:33,404
Sure. It's 580 won for 3.75 grams.

842
00:51:33,487 --> 00:51:35,864
[Mr. Jang] So ten of those is 5.8 mil,

843
00:51:35,948 --> 00:51:37,991
but that's only if this whole thing
is above board.

844
00:51:38,075 --> 00:51:41,078
I guess since you came to me,

845
00:51:41,161 --> 00:51:43,414
you can't sell it at
a regular jewelry store.

846
00:51:43,497 --> 00:51:44,915
[Mr. Jang] Am I right?

847
00:51:44,998 --> 00:51:48,460
My company, we can make a deal for 10.
100, even.

848
00:51:48,544 --> 00:51:51,755
If you're serious about selling
this thing, hop in. Then let's...

849
00:51:51,839 --> 00:51:52,923
Uh, I don't...

850
00:51:55,050 --> 00:51:56,260
I'll think about it a little more.

851
00:51:57,386 --> 00:51:59,513
You can't just bring this up
and then leave.

852
00:52:00,055 --> 00:52:01,640
At least let me have a look at it.

853
00:52:02,141 --> 00:52:03,809
-Let's see it.
-What?

854
00:52:03,892 --> 00:52:05,352
[Mr. Jang] Is it in the bag here?

855
00:52:05,436 --> 00:52:08,814
-I told you I'd give you a good deal!
-Let go!

856
00:52:08,897 --> 00:52:09,773
[Heeju] Stop it!

857
00:52:09,857 --> 00:52:11,358
[both shouting]

858
00:52:11,442 --> 00:52:14,778
[Mr. Jang] Ah, fuck, that stings!
[groans]

859
00:52:15,487 --> 00:52:17,740
Why is everyone such
a fucking bitch today?

860
00:52:18,449 --> 00:52:20,534
[groans]
STYLE
::cue()

861
00:52:20,617 --> 00:52:23,620
[breathing heavily]

862
00:52:25,247 --> 00:52:27,040
[Sunok] Where the hell have you been?

863
00:52:28,417 --> 00:52:30,753
[Sunok] Someone came asking
for you this morning. Some guy.

864
00:52:32,880 --> 00:52:33,881
Who was it?

865
00:52:33,964 --> 00:52:35,758
No idea.
That's why I'm asking.

866
00:52:36,675 --> 00:52:38,010
[Sunok] He said he lived in
the same town as us,

867
00:52:38,093 --> 00:52:39,261
but I don't recognize him.

868
00:52:39,928 --> 00:52:41,346
He seemed shady.

869
00:52:41,430 --> 00:52:44,141
Like one of those thugs who collect money
for loan sharks.

870
00:52:46,435 --> 00:52:48,061
-[Sunok] Did you borrow money?
-[exhales sharply]

871
00:52:48,145 --> 00:52:49,688
Tell me you haven't been gambling.

872
00:52:49,772 --> 00:52:51,023
No, I'm not like you.

873
00:52:51,607 --> 00:52:52,649
I would never.

874
00:52:54,485 --> 00:52:55,694
[Sunok inhales]

875
00:52:57,654 --> 00:52:58,864
[sips]

876
00:53:02,242 --> 00:53:03,327
[pill bottle rattles]

877
00:53:03,410 --> 00:53:04,703
TYLENOL

878
00:53:04,787 --> 00:53:05,996
What are you, sick?

879
00:53:06,955 --> 00:53:07,998
Have you been in pain?

880
00:53:08,081 --> 00:53:10,250
Doesn't matter.

881
00:53:10,334 --> 00:53:11,543
[exhales sharply]

882
00:53:13,045 --> 00:53:14,588
It's cancer, isn't it?

883
00:53:15,839 --> 00:53:17,633
Mija told you.

884
00:53:18,425 --> 00:53:19,760
Why didn't you tell me?

885
00:53:21,053 --> 00:53:22,888
You ran away 'cause you hate me.

886
00:53:24,223 --> 00:53:26,475
Then at least listen to Mija when
she tells you to go to the doctor.

887
00:53:26,558 --> 00:53:27,559
[Sunok] I did.

888
00:53:27,643 --> 00:53:28,894
I did go.

889
00:53:31,188 --> 00:53:33,982
Doctor said it was bone cancer
or something.

890
00:53:34,817 --> 00:53:35,818
[exhales]

891
00:53:37,194 --> 00:53:38,695
[Heeju] Then we have to go back.

892
00:53:38,779 --> 00:53:41,240
Go back so we can find out
what stage it is,

893
00:53:41,323 --> 00:53:43,075
what treatments there are,
if you need surgery.

894
00:53:43,826 --> 00:53:45,994
Are you sitting around here like
an idiot just because of money?

895
00:53:46,078 --> 00:53:47,162
What's with you?

896
00:53:47,246 --> 00:53:48,247
[exhales sharply]

897
00:53:49,790 --> 00:53:51,416
We're going to the hospital tomorrow.

898
00:53:51,500 --> 00:53:54,002
I don't even have money for food.

899
00:53:54,086 --> 00:53:56,630
We'll figure out a way to make
the money later.

900
00:53:56,713 --> 00:53:58,674
[Sunok] Oh, is that how it works?

901
00:54:00,425 --> 00:54:02,845
If life were that easy,
why are we here?

902
00:54:05,222 --> 00:54:07,307
[Sunok] I've looked into
it more than enough.

903
00:54:08,642 --> 00:54:10,686
The doctors said I
was better off not knowing.

904
00:54:12,479 --> 00:54:14,439
The surgery might get me
a few more years.

905
00:54:15,524 --> 00:54:19,111
Or I could die now.
What's the difference?

906
00:54:19,194 --> 00:54:20,904
We're all gonna die anyway.

907
00:54:22,447 --> 00:54:24,908
Oh, I'm tired of living like this.

908
00:54:25,909 --> 00:54:27,286
[exhales]

909
00:54:28,036 --> 00:54:30,581
Come on.
You don't really mean that, do you?

910
00:54:30,664 --> 00:54:33,208
We're going to the doctor tomorrow.

911
00:54:33,292 --> 00:54:34,626
Just let it go.

912
00:54:34,710 --> 00:54:38,463
You want me to call an ambulance?
I'm taking you one way or another.

913
00:54:38,547 --> 00:54:40,799
Be sure to lock the door
when you go to sleep.

914
00:54:40,883 --> 00:54:41,884
But...

915
00:54:43,343 --> 00:54:44,970
[groans]

916
00:54:45,053 --> 00:54:48,056
[door creaking]

917
00:54:50,267 --> 00:54:51,560
[exhales]
STYLE
::cue()

918
00:54:54,980 --> 00:54:57,983
[crickets chirping]

919
00:55:02,821 --> 00:55:04,364
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

920
00:55:04,448 --> 00:55:05,449
[car engine shuts off]

921
00:55:10,621 --> 00:55:11,830
[exhales]

922
00:55:11,913 --> 00:55:13,332
[glove compartment opens]

923
00:55:40,275 --> 00:55:43,278
[electricity quietly buzzing]

924
00:55:49,201 --> 00:55:50,911
[door creaking]

925
00:55:50,994 --> 00:55:52,287
[door clangs]

926
00:55:52,371 --> 00:55:55,540
[distant rattling]

927
00:55:55,624 --> 00:55:58,627
[door creaks quietly]

928
00:56:28,949 --> 00:56:30,867
[door creaking]

929
00:56:49,261 --> 00:56:51,763
[door knob clicking]

930
00:57:07,404 --> 00:57:08,613
[breathing erratically]

931
00:57:08,697 --> 00:57:11,241
-[Heeju] Who are you?
-Holy fuck, you scared me.

932
00:57:14,327 --> 00:57:15,704
You gotta be kidding.

933
00:57:15,787 --> 00:57:18,373
Everyone's walkin' around
with a gun lately.

934
00:57:18,457 --> 00:57:20,542
You know that shit's illegal, right?

935
00:57:20,625 --> 00:57:23,003
Get out or I'll scream.

936
00:57:23,086 --> 00:57:26,381
This isn't Seoul, Heeju.
You think anyone will come for you?

937
00:57:26,465 --> 00:57:27,883
I already called the police.

938
00:57:27,966 --> 00:57:29,593
[Woogy] Bullshit.

939
00:57:30,886 --> 00:57:33,096
The police?
You really want that?

940
00:57:33,180 --> 00:57:34,890
[gun rattling]

941
00:57:34,973 --> 00:57:37,058
We met a few days ago.

942
00:57:37,976 --> 00:57:39,603
[Woogy] And I almost fucking died.

943
00:57:41,938 --> 00:57:43,148
[exhales sharply]

944
00:57:44,816 --> 00:57:48,028
[Woogy] The person in the van.
It was you.

945
00:57:48,111 --> 00:57:50,322
At first I wasn't so sure.

946
00:57:50,781 --> 00:57:52,449
But when I saw you on the street,
I knew.

947
00:57:54,034 --> 00:57:56,495
Don't act like you know me.
You're not my friend.

948
00:57:56,578 --> 00:57:58,747
[exhales sharply]
Don't change the subject.

949
00:57:59,790 --> 00:58:00,874
Where's the casket?

950
00:58:02,751 --> 00:58:04,377
We found the van back at the warehouse.

951
00:58:05,462 --> 00:58:07,422
[Woogy] But the casket was missing.

952
00:58:08,799 --> 00:58:10,050
Tell me where it is.

953
00:58:10,133 --> 00:58:11,426
[shuddering]

954
00:58:11,510 --> 00:58:12,969
[Woogy] Ah.

955
00:58:14,679 --> 00:58:16,056
That it?

956
00:58:16,139 --> 00:58:17,724
[Heeju] Stay right there!

957
00:58:17,808 --> 00:58:19,142
I'm not afraid to shoot you.

958
00:58:20,936 --> 00:58:22,020
You sure it's loaded?

959
00:58:22,103 --> 00:58:24,147
You can find anything at a pawn shop.

960
00:58:24,231 --> 00:58:26,775
Do you really want to find out?

961
00:58:27,526 --> 00:58:28,527
Okay, okay.

962
00:58:28,610 --> 00:58:30,320
Yeah, I guess that's true.

963
00:58:31,613 --> 00:58:33,240
But just think for a sec.

964
00:58:34,157 --> 00:58:36,743
[Woogy] That stuff in the casket.
The drugs.

965
00:58:37,494 --> 00:58:38,578
Come on.

966
00:58:39,454 --> 00:58:40,664
[Woogy] Do you even know how to sell it?

967
00:58:41,581 --> 00:58:43,500
You can't do it alone.

968
00:58:43,583 --> 00:58:46,837
Lee Dokyung's basically crippled
after his accident.

969
00:58:46,920 --> 00:58:49,005
What good are the drugs to you, huh?

970
00:58:49,089 --> 00:58:50,799
[Woogy] If you can't sell 'em,
they're useless.

971
00:58:52,467 --> 00:58:54,553
-Heeju...
-[Heeju] I said don't move!

972
00:58:55,762 --> 00:58:57,305
I came here to help you out, Heeju.

973
00:58:57,806 --> 00:59:00,350
[Woogy] If I wanted to hurt you,
I would have brought the others.

974
00:59:00,433 --> 00:59:01,768
Let's just talk, yeah?

975
00:59:01,852 --> 00:59:04,396
Don't-don't move!
I swear I'll shoot you!

976
00:59:04,479 --> 00:59:05,397
Put the gun down.

977
00:59:05,480 --> 00:59:07,190
I told you to stay!
[whimpers]

978
00:59:07,274 --> 00:59:09,693
[Heeju groaning]

979
00:59:09,776 --> 00:59:11,027
[Woogy] Ah, shit.

980
00:59:11,111 --> 00:59:12,362
[gun cocks]

981
00:59:13,780 --> 00:59:16,575
I knew it.
You're a fuckin' liar.

982
00:59:22,831 --> 00:59:24,374
-Holy shit!
-[Heeju] No, wait.

983
00:59:24,457 --> 00:59:27,460
[Heeju grunting]

984
00:59:30,171 --> 00:59:32,132
[screams]

985
00:59:32,215 --> 00:59:33,842
[clattering]

986
00:59:33,925 --> 00:59:35,260
[Heeju whimpers]

987
00:59:36,219 --> 00:59:38,388
Look, I tried to be nice, but shit.

988
00:59:39,306 --> 00:59:41,349
I'll fucking shank you,
so stay down.
STYLE
::cue()

989
00:59:43,685 --> 00:59:44,936
[groans]

990
00:59:45,020 --> 00:59:48,481
Why the fuck is this thing so heavy?

991
00:59:48,565 --> 00:59:50,650
[bag thumping]

992
00:59:50,734 --> 00:59:53,737
[Heeju groaning]

993
00:59:55,864 --> 00:59:58,867
[Woogy grunting]

994
01:00:00,869 --> 01:00:02,537
[gold bars clink]

995
01:00:03,538 --> 01:00:06,374
[breathing heavily]

996
01:00:11,713 --> 01:00:13,548
[Woogy] Oh, fuck.

997
01:00:14,549 --> 01:00:15,550
Heeju.

998
01:00:17,636 --> 01:00:18,720
What is this?

999
01:00:20,931 --> 01:00:23,934
[Heeju breathing heavily]

1000
01:00:44,663 --> 01:00:47,666
[♪ tense music]

1001
01:01:07,727 --> 01:01:10,730
[♪ music continues]

